              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "समूहः — samūhaḥ — \"a group; a crowd\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "एकः समूहः शिबिरे साहाय्यं करोति। ekaḥ samūhaḥ śibire sāhāyyaṃ karoti. A group helps out in the camp."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A masculine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "समूहः (samūhaḥ) is built from sam, \"together\", and the root √ūh, \"to move, push\"; MW gives samūha as a collection, assemblage, multitude (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
